---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Sources from "../components/Sources.astro";
---
<Base title="Trust and safety · Amader Cloud" description="We never hold your money. Every app is reviewed against scams and impersonation. How we handle data, backups and broken changes.">

<section class="page-hero on-dark grid-night">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Trust and safety</p>
    <h1>Your money, your customers, your app.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Shared addresses like yourname.amader.cloud only work if people can trust them. Here is how we protect owners, their customers and everyone who clicks a link.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap pillars">
    <article class="card pillar" id="money">
      <span class="mono-label">01 · money</span>
      <h2>We never hold your money.</h2>
      <p>Payments go to your own merchant accounts through a licensed payment partner. Amader Cloud builds and hosts the app; we are never in the flow of funds, so we never sit on your sales and we don't need to be a payment company.</p>
      <ul class="ticks"><li>Your own bKash, Nagad and card merchant accounts</li><li>We help with the gateway paperwork</li><li>Your money is yours from the first order</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card pillar" id="review">
      <span class="mono-label">02 · review</span>
      <h2>Every app is checked before it goes live.</h2>
      <p>Free subdomains attract people who want to fake a bank or mobile-money page. So every app is reviewed by AI and rules before it is published, and again while it runs.</p>
      <ul class="ticks"><li>No impersonation of banks, payment brands, government or other businesses</li><li>Payment brand names can't be used in app names</li><li>No prohibited goods or scams</li><li>Takedown within hours when something slips through</li><li>A verified-business badge for owners who confirm who they are</li></ul>
      <p class="small">See something wrong on an amader.cloud address? <a href="contact.html?topic=abuse">Report it</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card pillar" id="changes">
      <span class="mono-label">03 · changes</span>
      <h2>A change can't quietly break your shop.</h2>
      <p>The AI builds on one fixed stack from tested components and connectors. Every change runs the tests and shows you a preview before it goes live, and any change can be rolled back in one click.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card pillar" id="data">
      <span class="mono-label">04 · data</span>
      <h2>Data and backups.</h2>
      <p>Your app's orders, customers and payment records are stored and backed up by us. You can export them at any time.</p>
      <ul class="ticks"><li>We process your customers' data on your behalf, under data-processing terms with you, in line with Bangladesh's Personal Data Protection Ordinance 2025</li><li>Building and editing use AI services and hosting that may be outside Bangladesh; our terms set out the basis for that transfer</li><li>An option to keep data hosted in Bangladesh is planned</li></ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="kicker">Being put in place for the beta</p>
      <h2>What we are still finishing.</h2>
      <p class="lede">We would rather show you the list than pretend it's done.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Agreement with a licensed payment aggregator, and its merchant onboarding</li>
      <li>An acceptable-use policy (impersonation, prohibited goods, scams), reviewed by a lawyer</li>
      <li>Data-processing terms for owners, including the cross-border basis for AI and hosting</li>
      <li>Rules on showing payment brand logos at checkout, agreed with the brands</li>
      <li>Company registration, trade licence and VAT registration</li>
      <li>Passing through the AI provider's usage policies to every app</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap"><Sources ids={["pdpo"]} /></div>
<div style="height:40px"></div>

<style>
.pillars { display: grid; gap: 22px; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
@media (max-width: 860px) { .pillars { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.pillar { padding: 28px; }
.pillar h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.1rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); }
.pillar .mono-label { background: var(--paper); }
.checklist { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; max-width: 820px; }
.checklist li { position: relative; padding: 12px 14px 12px 44px; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px; }
.checklist li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 14px; top: 15px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border: 1.5px dashed var(--bp-line); border-radius: 4px; }
</style>
</Base>
